WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.695
Hi, I'm Squiggle!

00:00:02.695 --> 00:00:08.783
Qwen3.8-Flash-Next has a hundred and twenty-five billion parameters and a fifty-one-billion lookup table.

00:00:08.783 --> 00:00:11.124
Six billion work per token.

00:00:12.392 --> 00:00:15.625
Four changes: attention, residual, embedding and optimiser.

00:00:15.625 --> 00:00:19.321
Each one chosen by its own controlled experiment.

00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:24.867
A token climbs forty-eight layers: three Gated DeltaNet, then one sparse

00:00:24.867 --> 00:00:26.394
attention, twelve times over.

00:00:26.394 --> 00:00:30.594
Every layer also picks ten of five hundred and twelve experts.

00:00:31.014 --> 00:00:33.946
DeltaNet keeps a fixed-size state, not a growing cache.

00:00:33.946 --> 00:00:38.506
It writes back only the error for each key: erase and rewrite, not append.

00:00:38.926 --> 00:00:43.463
But a finite state can't retrieve exactly, so every fourth layer attends globally.

00:00:43.883 --> 00:00:47.100
At layer two, a fifty-one-billion N-gram table joins in.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:51.390
Its lookups are known in advance, so they're prefetched from host memory.

00:00:53.167 --> 00:00:56.709
Sparse attention reads a fixed number of tokens, but its indexer

00:00:56.709 --> 00:00:57.998
still scans them all.

00:00:57.998 --> 00:01:00.896
At a million tokens, choosing costs more than reading.

00:01:01.316 --> 00:01:06.259
Qwen Sparse Attention compresses first, into micro-blocks, so that scan shrinks fourfold.

00:01:06.679 --> 00:01:09.923
It keeps the most relevant blocks, and attends only to those.

00:01:11.192 --> 00:01:16.018
Normally every layer writes into one residual stream, and early features get diluted.

00:01:16.438 --> 00:01:20.743
Gated Residual widens it to four lanes with gated reads and writes.

00:01:20.743 --> 00:01:23.614
One lane became a long-range path nobody designed.

00:01:24.842 --> 00:01:27.856
By training loss, the data-dependent gates looked like noise.

00:01:27.856 --> 00:01:31.875
By benchmark average, they beat the widening: one point nine eight points

00:01:31.875 --> 00:01:33.549
to one point five eight.

00:01:34.892 --> 00:01:38.253
The metric you can watch and the metric you want can diverge.

00:01:38.253 --> 00:01:39.373
This report says where.

00:01:43.692 --> 00:01:47.867
To recap: DeltaNet with sparse attention, four gated lanes, and a lookup

00:01:47.867 --> 00:01:49.954
table that lives off the GPU.

00:01:50.374 --> 00:01:52.520
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:53.133
I'm Squiggle.

00:01:53.133 --> 00:01:53.439
Bye!
